-- title:
--   Places over j=j₀ count pairs (E,C_N)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, let $N\ge 1$ (so $N$ is nonzero as a natural number) and assume $N\ne 0$ in $K$, and fix $j_0\in K$. Write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC K N` for the intermediate field of $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the set of all $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}_K\,d\,(j(q))$ with $d\mid N$, $d\ne 0$, where $j(q)=$ `jqModC K` is $q^{-1}$ times the power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-type unit `jNum` pushed to $K$; a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing $K$, distinct from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring, and $\operatorname{ord}_P$ denotes minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Let $S$ be a finite set of such places whose membership is characterised by the condition that $P\in S$ exactly when $\operatorname{ord}_P\bigl(j(q)-j_0\bigr)>0$. The conclusion is that the cardinality of $S$ equals the number of elements $x$ of `ModuliPoint N K` with `ModuliPoint.j x = j₀`, that is, of classes of pairs consisting of an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $K$ together with a point of exact additive order $N$, taken modulo variable changes combined with multiplication of the marked point by integers coprime to $N$, whose invariant `ModuliPoint.j` is $j_0$.
--
--   This is the modular interpretation of the $q$-expansion (Kroneckerian) model of $X_0(N)$ in characteristic not dividing $N$: the places of the full modular function field lying over a given value $j_0$ of the modular invariant correspond, without multiplicities, to the isomorphism classes of pairs consisting of an elliptic curve with $j$-invariant $j_0$ and a cyclic subgroup of order $N$. It is used in the counting arguments for the fibres of $X_0(N)\to X(1)$, in particular in the determination of the numbers of elliptic points and in the supersingular point count formulae.
